{% extends "tutorial_base.html.j2" %}

{% block tutorial_body %}
        <!-- Intro Card -->
        <div class="doc-intro-card">
          <h2>Heavy-Plate Piercing, Open-Path Kerf, Clean Remnants &amp; Zero Torch Dives</h2>
          <p>
            Thick plate, open trim cuts, and tight nests punish basic 2D CAM. Blowback wrecks nozzles on 1/2&Prime; steel, crossing an old kerf slot makes THC dive into the slats, and jagged skeletons waste half your sheet. These four primitives protect your consumables and squeeze more usable parts out of every plate.
          </p>
          <div class="doc-intro-grid">
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Void Crash Guard</span>
              <span class="value">0.5 &times; Kerf + 4.0 mm THC Lock</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Open &amp; Thick Plate</span>
              <span class="value">L/R/Center Kerf + Edge-Start</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Pro Sheet Pack</span>
              <span class="value">Guillotine Crop + Chain/Bridge</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 1
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-1">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 01</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Spatial Void THC Auto-Lock (<code class="mono">v0.8-A</code>: Zero Torch Dives)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              When a plasma torch crosses a previously cut kerf slot or pierce crater, arc voltage spikes and tricks Torch Height Control into diving the Z-axis straight into the steel.
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>RotaryCAM's <code class="mono">SpatialVoidIndex</code> records every cut kerf path and pierce crater automatically across both flat-sheet and rotary jobs.</li>
              <li>Whenever a later cut, common-line pass, or guillotine crop approaches within <code class="mono">0.5 &times; kerfWidth + 4.0 mm</code> of an existing void, the planner splits the <code class="mono">G1</code> segment.</li>
              <li>THC locks automatically through the crossing zone and unlocks only after the torch clears back onto solid metal. Zero manual kerf-crossing rules required.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 2
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-2">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 02</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Open-Path <code class="mono">Center / Left / Right</code> Kerf &amp; Thick-Plate <code class="mono">Edge-Start</code> (<code class="mono">Maker</code> &amp; <code class="mono">Pro Shop</code>)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Each control sits right inside the Features table where you tune individual contours:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li><strong>Open-Path Kerf (<code class="mono">Center (On-Line)</code> / <code class="mono">Left</code> / <code class="mono">Right</code>):</strong> Appears inline automatically in the Features table on unclosed DXF or SVG slit and trim lines (<code class="mono">is_centerline_slit</code>). Offset direction stays locked to the original stroke direction so trimmed plate edges hold exact finished size.</li>
              <li><strong><code class="mono">Edge-Start (Thick Plate)</code> Lead-In:</strong> Inside every feature's <code class="mono">Lead-In Strategy</code> dropdown. Selecting it reveals the <code class="mono">Edge Overhang</code> field (<code class="mono">4.0 mm</code> default) and flags an amber tip when cutting plate <code class="mono">&ge; 12 mm</code> (<code class="mono">1/2&Prime;</code>).</li>
              <li><strong>Safe Off-Plate Ignition:</strong> RotaryCAM probes IHS on solid steel at the contour start, retracts to pierce height, shifts off the plate edge by the overhang distance to fire without molten slag blowback, and locks THC until traveling <code class="mono">6.0 mm</code> onto solid steel.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 2: Features table showing inline Center (On-Line) / Left / Right kerf selector and Edge-Start (Thick Plate) lead-in</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/v08-open-path-edge-start.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/v08-open-path-edge-start.png" alt="Step 2: Open-path Center Left Right kerf control and Edge-Start Thick Plate lead-in dropdown" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 3
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-3">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 03</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Remnant Skeleton Guillotine Crop Cuts (<code class="mono">Pro Shop</code>)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Slice clean, square remnants off the back of your plate automatically instead of cutting freehand by eye:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>In flat-sheet <span class="ui-chip">Stock Nesting</span>, open the <span class="ui-chip">Guillotine Crop Cut</span> dropdown and pick <code class="mono">Best Single Cut</code>, <code class="mono">L-Cut (Both X &amp; Y)</code>, <code class="mono">Vertical (X)</code>, or <code class="mono">Horizontal (Y)</code>.</li>
              <li>Set the crop clearance margin (<code class="mono">kerf + 5.0 mm</code> default) to control how close the shear line runs to your nested parts.</li>
              <li>Inspect the dashed <code class="mono">CROP</code> path(s) and highlighted <code class="mono">Usable Remnant</code> area with exact dimensions inside the 2D Pack Part Preview before compiling G-code.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <figure class="doc-figure">
            <div class="doc-figure-bar">
              <span class="doc-figure-caption"><span class="dot"></span> Step 3: Flat-sheet Pack Mode with Guillotine Crop Cut, Usable Remnant preview, and Chain/Bridge options</span>
              <span class="doc-figure-zoom">🔍 Click image to enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-figure-img-wrap">
              <picture>
                <source srcset="assets/v08-flat-pro-pack.webp" type="image/webp" />
                <img src="assets/v08-flat-pro-pack.png" alt="Step 3: Flat-sheet Pack Mode showing Guillotine Crop Cut, Usable Remnant area, and Chain/Bridge cutting" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 4
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-4">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 04</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Serpentine <code class="mono">Daisy-Chain</code> &amp; <code class="mono">Micro-Bridge</code> Cutting (<code class="mono">Pro Shop</code>)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Cut pierces per sheet or keep lightweight parts tied to the skeleton in one continuous outer pass:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>Load the built-in <span class="ui-chip cyan">Flat Chain &amp; Bridge</span> fixture (<code class="mono">flat-chain-bridge-kit.svg</code>) from Quick CAD Fixtures to test on a multi-part layout.</li>
              <li>Uncheck <span class="ui-chip">Common-line cutting</span> first (Chain/Bridge and Common-Line modes are mutually exclusive in flat mode).</li>
              <li>Select <span class="ui-chip">Daisy-Chain (Single Pierce)</span> to link outer contours in a single continuous serpentine runner, or <span class="ui-chip">Micro-Bridge (Connected)</span> to keep parts anchored with narrow uncut tabs. Interior bolt holes always cut first before the chained outer pass starts.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>
{% endblock %}
